<title>UK: Rexam shares up after newspaper tip.</title>
<headline>Rexam shares up after newspaper tip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK print and packaging firm Rexam Plc climbed in pre-market trade on Monday after the Sunday Times newspaper said Rexam directors had been buying shares in the company and investors should consider following their lead.</p>
<p>&quot;Rolf Borjesson, its new chief executive, has made changes that could spark a change in fortunes,&quot; the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Rexam shares were two pence firmer at 239 by 0718 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
